零力交接把\"破裂瞬间冲击滑移\"换成\"舵机持续扛住弹性载荷\"——静置电流近:
The zero-force handover swaps "impact slip at the rupture instant" for "servos continuously holding the elastic load" — rest current nearly doubles, a trade-off that must go into the paper;
the weights push the steady-state load back down by about 20%, in the same direction as the Appendix A model (steady-state internal stress −32%) at about half the magnitude.
Note that the three runs were at different voltages (7.88/7.69/7.51 V), so absolute values across runs are confounded; slopes and within-run trends are trustworthy.

① 吸上瞬间零预载（刚吸的腿是\"软肩膀\"——lift_gate 早已观察到）:
① Zero preload at the instant of attachment (a freshly attached leg is a "soft shoulder" — lift_gate observed this long ago);
② thereafter every 1 mm the body drops winds that leg up by 1 mm (servo command unchanged, anchor moved relative to the body);
the older the attachment the tighter the wind-up, so the six legs store different energies; ③ the wave window order happens to lift one of the "tightest-wound" legs each time;
seal rupture = cutting its taut rubber band, and the body drops until the added deformation of the other five legs catches it;
④ the next attachment locks in the dropped position.

