这是 <b>P4 整机目标态</b>的连接拓扑。图 1 电气：2S 电池经 XT:
This is the connection topology of the <b>P4 whole-robot target state</b>. Fig. 1 electrical: the 2S battery goes through the XT60 master switch into three branches
    (servos 7.4 V direct / Pi independent 5 V / pneumatics 12 V); control signals run over USB, GPIO and I2C;
    Fig. 1b relay: terminal-level wiring of the servo power master switch;
    Fig. 2 pneumatics: two pumps + vacuum tank + 1-in-6-out manifold form the vacuum bus, with 6 identical branches to the foot cups.

系统图是拓扑级，这张落到\"哪根线插哪个脚\"。泵/阀的真实 GPIO 取自\n:
The system diagram is topology level; this one goes down to "which wire goes into which pin". The real pump/valve GPIOs come from
    <code>software/hexapod/adhesion.py</code> (Pi5VacuumIO, fitted in P1): <b>valve L1 = GPIO5, pump A = GPIO20</b>;
    servo relay = <b>GPIO17</b> (<code>driver.py</code>, settled 08-15, previously Servo2040 A0/GPIO26);
    the other 6 MOSFET control lines are a suggested allocation (settled at P4 assembly), avoiding the I2C1 / UART / SPI0 / ID-EEPROM / PWM-audio pins.

本项目用的是第三种。舵机自己内部还分好几个大类（模拟 / 数字 / 总线 / 关:
This project uses the third kind. Servos themselves split into several families (analog / digital / bus / joint module,
    plus three motion types: limited, continuous rotation, multi-turn), expanded in <strong>Section 3</strong>;
    what switching to another type would mean for this machine is costed in <strong>Section 10</strong>.

差别不在信号（都吃同样的脉宽），在内部：模拟舵机大约按 50Hz 的节奏驱动电机:
The difference is not in the signal (both take the same pulse width) but inside: an analog servo drives the motor at roughly the 50 Hz rhythm, with a large dead band, jitter and weak holding force;
    a digital servo drives at several hundred Hz internally, with <strong>a small dead band, fast response and clearly higher holding torque</strong>, at the cost of more current and heat.
    Joints must use digital servos — on the wall every stance leg carries shear load continuously, and that holding torque is what it relies on.

各家型号更新很快，记类别比记型号有用。举几个常见的当搜索入口：\n 模拟档:
Models change fast, so remembering the category is more useful than remembering models. Some common ones as search entry points:
    analog: the SG90, MG996R family; digital: DS3218 / DS3235 / ZOSKAY, high-end RC is Savox, Futaba;
    bus servos: Feetech SCS / STS series, Hiwonder LX-16A, and the most complete but priciest ecosystem, Robotis Dynamixel;
    joint modules: Unitree GO-M8010, DaMiao DM-J4310, MyActuator RMD-X, the ones used in quadruped robot dogs.

舵机不认识\"度\"。它只认<b>脉宽</b>:每 20ms 给它一个 500~:
Servos do not know "degrees". They only know <b>pulse width</b>: a 500–2500 µs high pulse every 20 ms;
the width of the pulse sets the horn angle, and the internal potentiometer closes the loop. So the last step is looking up each servo's calibration
(18 ServoCal entries in config.py, all measured and fitted on 2026-08-08):

决定这台机器能不能上墙的，全是\"不像机器人学\"的东西：一个接头没插到底，机器:
What decides whether this machine gets onto the wall is all "un-robotics-like": a fitting not pushed fully home and the robot drops;
      a bit less power margin and it reboots in mid-air; a wrong calibration reference and "stand perpendicular" comes out tilted;
      nobody thinks of the cup's elastic energy storage and four days of tuning go nowhere. There is no textbook for these; only measurement, records and cross-examination.

